<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cairo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cairo is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, founded in 969 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> as their capital, next to the older settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fustat">Fustat</a>. It was the seat of the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>, and after 1261 hosted a line of Abbasid caliphs under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> protection. Cairo became one of the largest and wealthiest cities of the medieval Islamic world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cairo.jpg" alt="Cairo" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jorge Láscar from Melbourne, Australia · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cairo_Opera_House,_Al_Hurriyah_Park_and_the_Nile_river_(14797782354).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
